    verification scriptsResolveModuleHomesReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "727e13cf-d3fd-42cd-9c18-bf757f40cc7b"; :>> title = "Sprint 719 review gate — three passes per D0172"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-15"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Three passes (D0172). Correctness: module_home refuses ambiguity rather than picking a crate, returns None rather than raising for an absent module so each caller keeps its own failure text, and reads the member list from the manifest so a new member needs no edit; the Rust corpus falls back to keel-cli/src only when no root manifest exists, so an engine run at a foreign root still says why. Honesty: the two D0360 instruments disagreed after the script alone was widened (58/17 against 55/20) and agree again only after the binary's corpus moved too - widening one instrument and not the other would have left a false disagreement standing; facts.py's cliFamilyCensus had been null on every brief since sprint 714 took cli_facts.rs into keel-schema, and is computed again. Scope: no view, guard or write-path change; modgraph.py keeps keel-cli/src as its documented default because its graph is of that crate's modules and a moved module leaves the graph rather than breaking it. Control added (D0047): module_home.py --probe scans for the anchor shape and runs in the CI script-probe step"; }
    // RAN: Three passes (D0172) over the diff at d110d0a plus the working tree. Correctness: module_home() raises AmbiguousModule naming both homes on two hits and returns None on none (scripts/module_home.py; probe cases both_rs ambiguity and MISSING); crate_dirs reads Cargo.toml [workspace] members through tomllib with glob expansion and normpath (the first probe run failed on mixed separators for members/keel-write and was fixed there); control_proof.rs corpus_bodies falls back to keel-cli/src only with no root manifest, and the fixture test proves undetermined()==1 without the manifest and proven()==1 with it. Honesty: after the script alone was widened the two D0360 instruments disagreed (census 58 named / 17 unnamed vs binary 55 / 20); both now read one corpus and agree at 915 test functions / 32 / 26 / 17 - widening one instrument and not the other would have left a false disagreement standing; facts.py's cliFamilyCensus had been null on every brief since sprint 714 took cli_facts.rs into keel-schema and is computed again. Scope: no view, guard or write-path change; modgraph.py keeps keel-cli/src as its documented default because its graph is of that crate's modules. Control added (D0047): module_home.py --probe scans scripts/**/*.py and .engine/tools/*.py for the two anchor shapes and runs in the CI script-probe step (D0394); declared as Sensor snModuleHome with its known failure modes (a third anchor shape passes the scan - a miss, never a false positive).
