    verification scriptsResolveModuleHomesRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "06216701-c8c5-48b3-bef4-257dcd9b94ba"; :>> title = "Sprint 719 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-15"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Retro, avoidable-issue scan over the sprint: (1) the standup line of sprint 718 named receipt_shape_census.py:14 as a path that followed the move - that was the docstring; the constant three lines below the imports did not, so a grep for the file name was read as a grep for the anchor. The control that catches the shape rather than the name is this sprint's scan - no new item. (2) The CI script-probe step (D0394) is the only place the probe scripts run; keel verify's ladder does not include them, so the defect reached the remote before anything local fired. A local rung for the script probes is a process change to the ladder - tracked as dcScriptProbesRunInTheVerifyLadder (chartered by D0476), not done here. (3) The two D0360 instruments agreed while both were wrong the same way; agreement is not correctness, and the census reference must read a corpus it derives (the manifest) rather than one it names - fixed here, no new item. (4) facts.py emitted cliFamilyCensus as null on every brief built since sprint 714 moved cli_facts.rs the same morning (87085d2), under an except OSError whose how-text read as a computed absence; a null with a reason is honest only when the reason is the fact's, not a missing file's - the resolver returns None and the caller's how-text now names the module and the list it was resolved against, no new item. (5) AVOIDABLE: the Review and DoD claims about facts.py were read from the edit, not from a run - facts.py died at HEAD on that edit; issue560 (High), resolver dcInstrumentAnswersCarryTheirSourceHash, delivered by sprint 720 (an answer carries its instrument hash and the reader refuses drift)"; }
